.Dd June 1, 2025
.Dt XO_IS_EMITTING 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xo_is_emitting , xo_is_emitting_h
.Nd test whether libxo will emit output at the current position
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxo
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libxo/xo.h
.Ft int
.Fn xo_is_emitting "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xo_is_emitting_h "xo_handle_t *xop"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
When a filter is active, the current output hierarchy may be permanently
filtered out: the filtering software has determined that no further
content generated here can ever appear in the final output.
.Pp
The
.Fn xo_is_emitting
function returns true when output at the current position of the default
handle will reach the final output.
Callers can use this to skip expensive computation that would otherwise
precede a call to
.Xr xo_emit 3 .
.Pp
The
.Fn xo_is_emitting_h
variant operates on the specified handle.
To use the default handle, pass a
.Dv NULL
handle.
.Pp
Both functions return true when filtering is disabled, when the filter
module is not loaded, or when the filter status does not indicate a
permanent filtering state.
Both functions return false only when the filter has permanently
discarded the current output position.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns true
.Pq non-zero
when output at the current position will reach the final output.
Returns false
.Pq zero
when the filter has permanently discarded the current output position.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xo_open_container("some-parent");
if (xo_is_emitting()) {
    xo_open_container("connections");
    xo_emit("{:field/...}", value);
    /* Massive content generation */
    xo_close_container("connections");
}
xo_close_container("some-parent");
.Ed
.Pp
For example,
.Dq my-app --libxo filter=!some-parent
means that when
.Nm libxo
sees the
.Dq some-parent
tag, it knows that nothing under that container will be emitted.
By calling
.Fn xo_is_emitting ,
the code avoids the expense of massive content generation.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr xo_add_filter 3 ,
.Xr xo_emit 3 ,
.Xr xo_filter 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn xo_is_emitting
function first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.Nm libxo
was written by
.An Phil Shafer Aq Mt phil@freebsd.org .
